{
  "centralMessage": "Real virtues can enable exploitation when power allocates their costs asymmetrically; universal cynicism evades evidence and may train the critic to exploit the vulnerabilities he understands. The fictional narrator is tested when observation becomes decision-making power, with no final guarantee of innocence.",
